---
// Mount point for lesson 15's address board. The intro is server-rendered so the
// lesson still says something without JavaScript, and so the opening copy lives
// in one place. Everything after the button is built at runtime by
// src/scripts/courses/addresses/addresses.ts.
import "@styles/addresses.css";
---

<div data-addresses>
  <div class="ab not-prose my-8">
    <div data-ab-stage>
      <div class="ab-shell">
        <div class="ab-intro">
          <p>
            Three nodes, a shop and an api. Somebody copied the api pod's address
            into shop's config, and shop sends it a request every couple of seconds.
            Do things to the cluster and watch where the requests end up.
          </p>
          <div class="ab-foot">
            <button type="button" class="ab-btn" data-tone="primary" data-go="start"
              >Open the cluster</button
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p class="ab-note mt-3">
        This board needs JavaScript. The short version: shop reaches the api pod on
        another node directly, and the api pod sees shop's own address. Crash the
        api container and it still works, because it's the same pod. Delete the pod,
        ship a new version or remove its node, and the replacement comes up with a
        different address while shop keeps sending to the old one.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import "@scripts/courses/addresses/addresses";
</script>
